<title>FRANCE: French March health spending up 0.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>French March health spending up 0.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monthly health spending in France rose 0.6 percent in March from February but was unchanged for the first quarter of 1997 compared to the same period in 1996, the CNAM national health insurance fund said.</p>
<p>Monthly spending excluding public hospitals rose 1.3 percent, while doctors fees were up 1.8 percent, CNAM said in a statement.</p>
<p>Prescription rose 1.3 percent overall, while spending on private hospitals was up 1.8 percent.</p>
<p>The CNAM did not give figures in Francs as it has in previous months.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
